            <h3 data-number="4.3.2" id="content-elements"><span
            class="header-section-number">4.3.2</span> Content
            elements</h3>
            <p>The LIDO element descriptions distinguish between the
            following kinds of content elements:</p>
            <ol type="1">
            <li>Text elements for free-text notes</li>
            <li>Display elements, a kind of text elements</li>
            <li>Index elements holding indexing terms</li>
            <li>Identifier elements for all kinds of entities</li>
            </ol>
            <h4 data-number="4.3.2.1" id="text-elements"><span
            class="header-section-number">4.3.2.1</span> Text
            elements</h4>
            <p><strong>Note:</strong> In the <a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html">LIDO
            Schema Documentation</a>, an element is introduced as “A
            text element …” if it is intended to present human-readable
            notes or explanations, populated with free-text data values.
            Most of the text elements are used for display and source
            information, or for more detailed textual descriptions of
            the object or work. Note that exactly one
            &lt;lido:appellationValue&gt; per language should be marked
            as the preferred one.</p>
            <p><strong>Features:</strong> Defined by <a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#textComplexType"><em>textComplexType</em></a>,
            a text element can have attributes, is repeatable (under
            conditions), and has free text (xs:string) as its data
            value.</p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong> &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#appellationValue">lido:appellationValue</a>&gt;
            is a text element contained by several elements for naming
            entities. This element is required if an element for naming
            entities is used, e.g., &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#nameActorSet">lido:nameActorSet</a>&gt;.</p>
            <blockquote>
            <p><strong>Creator:</strong> Leonardo da Vinci
            <strong><em>Preference:</em></strong> Preferred</p>
            </blockquote>
            <div class="sourceCode" id="cb13"><pre
            class="sourceCode xml"><code class="sourceCode xml"><span id="cb13-1"><a href="#cb13-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;<span class="kw">lido:nameActorSet</span>&gt;</span>
<span id="cb13-2"><a href="#cb13-2" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>    &lt;<span class="kw">lido:appellationValue</span></span>
<span id="cb13-3"><a href="#cb13-3" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a><span class="ot">        lido:pref=</span><span cla